{"id":"9e745949a6ee96af","group":"68","path":"68/68-thm-universal-function-theorem.md","title":"Universal Function Theorem","display":"thm-universal-function-theorem — Universal Function Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)","book_abbrev":"68","label":"68-thm-universal-function-theorem","aliases":["68-thm-universal-function-theorem"],"display":"thm-universal-function-theorem — Universal Function Theorem","depends_on":["[[68-df-number-theoretic-function]]","[[68-df-kleene-normal-form]]","[[68-df-pairing-function]]","[[68-thm-basic-machine-characterization]]"],"source_edition":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF","source_location":"§8.2 p.22 / PDF 31","verification_status":"source-adapted-and-derived","source_proof_status":"source-proof-and-adaptation-reviewed","revision_basis":"supplied-68(1).zip; local content, type, and dependency review"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"68"},{"key":"label","html":"68-thm-universal-function-theorem"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>68-thm-universal-function-theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-universal-function-theorem — Universal Function Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c524671590651be2\" href=\"?note=c524671590651be2\" title=\"68-df-number-theoretic-function\">68-df-number-theoretic-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"bca7d0eca4017dc7\" href=\"?note=bca7d0eca4017dc7\" title=\"68-df-kleene-normal-form\">68-df-kleene-normal-form</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"a3970a22e73ed3ca\" href=\"?note=a3970a22e73ed3ca\" title=\"68-df-pairing-function\">68-df-pairing-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"d018b8faa50481e8\" href=\"?note=d018b8faa50481e8\" title=\"68-thm-basic-machine-characterization\">68-thm-basic-machine-characterization</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF"},{"key":"source_location","html":"§8.2 p.22 / PDF 31"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-adapted-and-derived"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"source-proof-and-adaptation-reviewed"},{"key":"revision_basis","html":"supplied-68(1).zip; local content, type, and dependency review"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PartRec}\">\\(\\mathrm{PartRec}\\)</span> 与多元索引 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi_e^{(k)}\">\\(\\varphi_e^{(k)}\\)</span> 的对应见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"d018b8faa50481e8\" href=\"?note=d018b8faa50481e8\" title=\"68-thm-basic-machine-characterization\">68-thm-basic-machine-characterization</a>、<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"bca7d0eca4017dc7\" href=\"?note=bca7d0eca4017dc7\" title=\"68-df-kleene-normal-form\">68-df-kleene-normal-form</a>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{pair}\">\\(\\mathrm{pair}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"a3970a22e73ed3ca\" href=\"?note=a3970a22e73ed3ca\" title=\"68-df-pairing-function\">68-df-pairing-function</a>。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(k\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>。</p>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"e\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(e\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vec x\\in\\mathbb N^k\">\\(\\vec x\\in\\mathbb N^k\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\langle e\\rangle\\,^{\\frown}\\vec x\\in\\mathbb N^{k+1}\">\\(\\langle e\\rangle\\,^{\\frown}\\vec x\\in\\mathbb N^{k+1}\\)</span>。连接算子与 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal F_k\">\\(\\mathcal F_k\\)</span> 的元数约定见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"c524671590651be2\" href=\"?note=c524671590651be2\" title=\"68-df-number-theoretic-function\">68-df-number-theoretic-function</a>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\exists v\\in\\mathrm{PartRec}\\cap\\mathcal F_{k+1}\\;\\forall e\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\forall\\vec x\\in\\mathbb N^k\\;(v(\\langle e\\rangle\\,^{\\frown}\\vec x)\\simeq\\varphi_e^{(k)}(\\vec x)).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\forall k\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\exists v\\in\\mathrm{PartRec}\\cap\\mathcal F_{k+1}\\;\\forall e\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\forall\\vec x\\in\\mathbb N^k\\;(v(\\langle e\\rangle\\,^{\\frown}\\vec x)\\simeq\\varphi_e^{(k)}(\\vec x)).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\exists u\\in\\mathrm{PartRec}\\cap\\mathcal F_1\\;\\forall e,x\\in\\mathbb N\\;(u(\\mathrm{pair}(e,x))\\simeq\\varphi_e(x)).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\exists u\\in\\mathrm{PartRec}\\cap\\mathcal F_1\\;\\forall e,x\\in\\mathbb N\\;(u(\\mathrm{pair}(e,x))\\simeq\\varphi_e(x)).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>8.2 Enumeration Theorem，印刷 p.22 / PDF p.31。原书证明直接将 e 视为 Normal Form 的额外输入；第二式由第一式及 Cantor 配对的可计算逆得到。本目录先前只有一元配对版本，这里补齐书中的任意元数版本。u 是偏递归的；不可要求 u 为全函数。已核对原书证明，Cantor 编码替换是本地推导。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"68-df-number-theoretic-function","status":"resolved","id":"c524671590651be2","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[68-df-number-theoretic-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"68-df-kleene-normal-form","status":"resolved","id":"bca7d0eca4017dc7","